          "locator": "ch. XXIII, paragraph beginning \"In a general sense, then, it may be said that, when daylight showed...\"",
          "quote": "In a general sense, then, it may be said that, when daylight showed the enemies to each other, the British fleet was heading to the northward, and that of the allies to the southward; the latter being ten or twelve miles east of their opponents. In the far distance, Cape Trafalgar, from which the battle takes its name, was just visible against the eastern sky."
