          "source": "mahan",
          "locator": "ch. XXIII, paragraph beginning \"The \"Victory,\" always a fast ship, had likewise little difficulty...\"",
          "quote": "Blackwood, having failed to get Nelson on board his own frigate, and realizing the exposure inseparable from the position of leader, ventured, at about half-past nine, when still six miles from the enemy, to urge that one or two ships should be permitted to precede the \"Victory.\""
