      "caption": "Just at noon the Fougueux fires the first gun of the battle at the Royal Sovereign, and for ten minutes Collingwood advances in silence, the one centre of the hostile fire. At ten minutes past twelve he breaks through astern of the Santa Ana; the Victory is two miles off, with a mile and a half still to go.",
      "notes": "Both times are exact. The Royal Sovereign's breaking point is placed on the southern half of the allied crescent, about 1.9 nmi from the Victory and roughly two-thirds of the way from the allied centre to the southern horn - Mahan names the Santa Ana as her opponent but gives no station number, so the exact point is an estimate consistent with the two miles between the flagships and with the attack falling on the rear. The lee column's own centre is drawn about 1.6 nmi astern of the Royal Sovereign, who \"easily took the lead\" and was well ahead of her division. State for the lee column steps to engaged at this instant; the weather column is not yet under effective fire, so it holds at intact.",
